From f71b65ae74280f84da7186fa5e7fed409c38f325 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:46:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: qcom-hw: Add SDM660 OSM programming

The SDM660 OSM runs the TrustZone owned sequencer like MSM8998 but is
programmed as clk-cpu-osm-660.c of the vendor kernel does. Add a
qcom,sdm660-cpufreq-hw variant that follows the vendor driver and the
vendor device tree configuration:

- Wait for the L2 SAWs listed in qcom,saw, which pass the CPRh voltage
  requests to the PMIC, then set the GPLL0 based alternate clock (LUT
  index 0) to 300 MHz and the APCS OSM clock RCG to 200 MHz from it
  (source 1, divider 1.5) before any OSM register is written.
- Attach the CPU to the CPRh power domain first, so the CPRh is fully
  programmed before the OSM, then write the cycle counter, all 40 LUT
  rows (the last entry fills the rest), the CC and LLM policies and the
  FSM timers in OSM clock cycles, with the vendor read-modify-write
  semantics and no PC override index.
- Derive the MEM-ACC thresholds from the corners where the LUT spare data
  changes, keeping missing transitions at corner 0 as the vendor driver
  does instead of requiring two crossovers, and write the L-val of the
  first corner of the highest MEM-ACC level.
- Write the APM threshold corner (not the crossover corner) to SEQ_REG1,
  and the crossover, threshold, previous-corner (0xff below corner 1) and
  APM parameter sequencer registers through SCM.
- Request index 0 before enabling the OSM. Any error leaves it disabled.
- On any programming error, detach the CPU from the CPRh domain again
  (and free the parameter table), so that the next CPU of the domain
  retries from a clean state instead of finding a stale attachment.
- No ACD and no bandwidth votes on frequency changes.

The LUT, MEM-ACC and APM values are logged when the OSM is programmed.

An optional qcom,lut-max-microvolt property keeps LUT entries above that
voltage out of the cpufreq frequency table, so they are never requested
while the hardware still has the full table.

Scope: SDM630/660 common
Porting notes: Local addition based on the vendor crDroid 4.19 drivers/clk/qcom/clk-cpu-osm-660.c and the clock_cpu node of arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/qcom/sdm660.dtsi (not upstream).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/qcom-cpufreq-hw.c | 494 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 469 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

